Requirements for BigTranslate

REQUIREMENTS:

* Java Development Kit (JDK) 21
* JAVA_HOME set
* Python 3.10+
* Pantogloss importable (`from pantogloss import Translator`)
* libmagic
* Mnemosyne (resolved from Maven Central; the version is pinned by
  `oodt.version` in the root pom, so it is not repeated here)

Current walkthrough: https://github.com/chrismattmann/bigtranslate/wiki/Installation

INSTALLATION:

# build oodt
	$ mvn clean package <OPTIONAL PROFILES>		# see optional build profiles below

# The oodt install 

# deploy oodt
	$ tar zxf distribution/target/${PROJECT_ARTIFACT_ID}-distribution-*-bin.tar.gz -C /my/deployment/directory/oodt


NOTE:
Optinal Build Profiles:  
For other build configurations, add the following arguments:
  	(default)           : bin, crawler, data, extensions,
                        filemgr (Lucene), logs, pcs, resmgr,
                        tomcat, workflow, pge

  	-Pfm-solr-catalog   : default components, filemgr (Solr),
                        solr, tomcat/webapps/solr


RUN:

  $ cd /my/deployment/directory/oodt
  $ cd bin
  $ ./oodt start


 START BigTranslate:

 
Ingest file

$ cd $OODT_HOME/crawler/bin;
$ ./crawler_launcher --operation --metPC --productPath $BIGTRANSLATE_HOME/data/staging --metExtractorConfig $BIGTRANSLATE_HOME/extractors/default/default.cpr.conf --metExtractor org.apache.oodt.cas.metadata.extractors.CopyAndRewriteExtractor --filemgrUrl $FILEMGR_URL --clientTransferer org.apache.oodt.cas.filemgr.datatransfer.InPlaceDataTransferFactory

Send an event to the Workflow Manager to start the extract, which reads the
catalogued corpus once and writes the chunks the translate stage works on.
bin/bigtranslate translate does this for you after its crawl.

 $ cd $OODT_HOME/workflow/bin;
 $ ./wmgr-client --url $WORKFLOW_URL --operation --sendEvent --eventName EmploymentCorpusReady
